{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LeverLogDerivative","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LeverLogDerivative","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Inv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LeverLogDerivative.cube_lever_gate_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LeverLogDerivative.cube_lever_gate_form","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LeverLogDerivative.lean#L39-L46","doc":"The decomposition rewritten in gate form: the *un-levered* derivative of\nthe ratio recovers `f′` up to the log-derivative correction —\n`u³·(d/dq)(f/u³) = f′ − 3(u′/u)·f`.  This is the identity behind\n\"`u³·d[Im 𝔙(m(q))]/dq ≈ A′` at an anchor\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LeverLogDerivative.hasDerivAt_div_pow_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LeverLogDerivative.hasDerivAt_div_pow_three","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LeverLogDerivative.lean#L25-L37","doc":"**Quotient-rule decomposition for a cube-lever ratio.**  If `f` and `u`\nare differentiable at `q` with `u q ≠ 0`, then `f/u³` is differentiable at\n`q` with derivative `f′/u³ − 3(u′/u)(f/u³)` — the exact algebraic shape of\nthe c₃ S-slope decomposition (`f = A`, `S − Vol(4₁) = A/u³`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}